## Tracker state
Table `Applications` includes `Role_Category` + `Subrole_Categories` (was `Role_Categories`); `Confirmation_#` removed. Location columns are free text. List DVs are **table-body only** (not whole-column); HTP syncs editable + code-owned lists (`Work_Mode`, `Employment_Type`, `Outcome`, `Role_Category`, …) on write. User keeps the workbook closed while the engine writes.
`Employment_Type` labels: Permanent Full-/Part-time, Contract (+ Full-/Part-Time), Internship Full-/Part-time, Co-op Full-/Part-time, Temporary, Freelance, Unknown.
One-time migrations live under `scripts/one_time/` (`python -m scripts.one_time.migrate_locations|migrate_role_category|migrate_employment_type`; Excel closed).

## Testing conventions
- `python -m pytest` is the first check after any backend change; `cd frontend && npx vue-tsc --noEmit` after frontend changes.
- Manual runs: never against the real tracker; copy it to `%TEMP%\htp_ui`, write a config there (incl. `candidate_context_path` to a fictional context) and set `HTP_CONFIG`.
- Start the API without `--reload` from a background shell when testing from the agent; restart it after backend edits. Seed sessions/files via the API since the Cursor browser cannot pick files.
- Keep scratch tests outside the repo; `git status` must stay clean of test artifacts. Remove `%TEMP%\htp_ui` afterwards.

